\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 1 & 0 & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 7 & & \\
\cline{3-4}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 0 & \\
\end{array}$$

The decimal representation of $\frac47$ is $0.\overline{571428}$. Since this pattern repeats every 6 digits, the 125th digit after the decimal point will be the same as the 125th digit in the pattern $571428$. Since $125 \div 6 = 20$ with a remainder of 5, the 125th digit is the same as the 5th digit in the pattern, which is $\boxed{2}$.The answer is: 2

