solution_steps:
The number of ways to get heads in exactly $k$ flips out of 10 is $\binom{10}{k}$,
so the probability of getting exactly $k$ heads is $\binom{10}{k}(1/2)^{10}$.
The probability of getting heads in at least 8 of the 10 flips is
\[\binom{10}{8}(1/2)^{10} + \binom{10}{9}(1/2)^{10} + \binom{10}{10}(1/2)^{10}
= \frac{45+10+1}{2^{10}} = \frac{56}{1024} = \boxed{\frac{7}{128}}.\]
The answer is: \frac{7}{128}

